1. MENTAL MODEL
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 
  A vault is just a folder of .md files. No database, no lock-in.
  Obsidian is a renderer + link graph on top of plain files.
 
  Anything you can do with grep, ripgrep, sed, or git works on a vault.
  Config lives in <vault>/.obsidian/ (JSON). Everything else is yours.
 
  Editing modes:
    Reading view    rendered output
    Live Preview    renders inline, shows raw syntax at cursor  (default)
    Source mode     raw markdown always
  Toggle read/edit: Ctrl+E   Toggle Live Preview/Source: Settings > Editor
 
 
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. LINKS, EMBEDS, BLOCKS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 
  [[Note Name]]                  wikilink
  [[Note Name|Display text]]     wikilink with alt display text
  [[Note#Heading]]               link to a heading in a note
  [[Note#Head#Subhead]]          link to a nested heading
  [[Note#^abc123]]               link to a specific block
  [[#Heading]]                   link to heading in the CURRENT note
  [text](Note%20Name.md)         standard markdown link (also works)
  [text](https://example.com)    external link
 
  ![[Note Name]]                 embed (transclude) an entire note
  ![[Note#Heading]]              embed just that section
  ![[Note#^abc123]]              embed just that block
  ![[image.png]]                 embed an image
  ![[image.png|400]]             embed image, width 400px
  ![[image.png|400x300]]         embed image, fixed w x h
  ![[doc.pdf#page=3]]            embed a PDF at a page
  ![[clip.mp4]]                  embed audio/video
 
  Block IDs: append ^someid to the END of a paragraph or list item.
 
      This is the paragraph I want to reference. ^design-note
 
  Typing [[Note#^ then picking from the autocomplete generates the ID
  for you.
 
  Unresolved links (target does not exist yet) show dimmed. Clicking one
  creates the note. This is the fastest way to outline a vault.
 
  Aliases in frontmatter make [[alias]] resolve to the real note.
 
 
