5. PROPERTIES (YAML FRONTMATTER)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 
  Must be the very first thing in the file, fenced by ---
 
    ---
    title: XCP vs DobiMigrate SMB Lab
    aliases:
      - xcp lab
      - smb migration lab
    tags:
      - lab
      - datadobi
    status: active
    date: 2026-07-24
    reviewed: false
    cssclasses:
      - wide-page
    ---
 
  Property types Obsidian understands: Text, List, Number, Checkbox,
  Date, Date & time. Type is set per-property-name vault-wide.
 
  Reserved / special keys:
    tags        adds tags without inline #tag
    aliases     alternate names that resolve in [[ ]] and quick switcher
    cssclasses  applies CSS classes to that note
    publish     used by Obsidian Publish
 
  Dates use YYYY-MM-DD. Datetimes use YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ss.
  Bare true/false become checkboxes. Quote them if you want text.
 
  Cmd/Ctrl+; ... actually: use the command palette > "Add file property".
 
 
