15. GOTCHAS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 
  * Renaming a note updates every [[wikilink]] to it automatically.
    Renaming the FILE outside Obsidian does not. Rename inside the app,
    or fix links yourself.
 
  * Moving a file changes markdown-style links if "Use [[Wikilinks]]"
    is off. Wikilinks are path-independent by default, which is usually
    what you want. Settings > Files and links.
 
  * "New link format" setting: shortest path / relative / absolute.
    Shortest path breaks if two notes share a filename in different
    folders. Absolute is safest for large vaults.
 
  * Frontmatter must be at line 1. A blank line above it silently
    breaks it into a plain horizontal rule.
 
  * Tags in YAML: use tags:, not tag:. Both forms below work.
        tags: [a, b]
        tags:
          - a
          - b
 
  * Attachments default to the vault root. Set a dedicated folder early
    (Settings > Files and links > Default location for new attachments)
    or you will be sorting 400 pasted PNGs later.
 
  * Live Preview hides syntax at the cursor line only. If something
    renders wrong, drop to Source mode (Ctrl+P > "Toggle source mode")
    to see the raw text.
 
  * Sync: Obsidian Sync is paid and handles conflicts well. iCloud and
    Dropbox work but can corrupt on concurrent edits. Git is free and
    explicit but is a manual conflict resolver on mobile.
 
